    "result_text": "All tests pass. The full suite (3 tests) is green and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization for owner creation (`POST /api/owners`), following the existing OfficeFloor function-injection patterns (`NormalizeOwnerTelephone`/`NormalizeOwnerEmail`).\n\n**New files:**\n- `AddressNormalizer.java` \u2014 shared, idempotent utility: trims and collapses whitespace, upper-cases, and expands whole-token abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). `null`/whitespace-only \u2192 `\"\"`.\n- `NormalizeOwnerAddress.java` \u2014 a pipeline step that writes the canonical address back onto the shared request DTO, so it's stored and returned (via the mapper \u2192 `Owner`).\n\n**Changed files:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `normalizeAddress` step after email normalization, before the uniqueness/build steps (so both storage and every downstream address comparison see the normalized form).\n- `RequireOwnerFields.java` \u2014 the address required-field check now rejects an address that is **blank after normalization** (via `AddressNormalizer.normalize(...).isEmpty()`), covering both missing and whitespace-only.\n- `RequireUniqueHousehold.java` and `AssignHouseholdId.java` \u2014 the **address** side of duplicate detection and the shared household-id derivation now compare using `AddressNormalizer.normalize(...)` on both the request and each existing owner, so comparisons are robust even against non-normalized stored/seed addresses.\n\nThe three acceptance tests (`\"  12  main  st \"\u2192\"12 MAIN STREET\"`, `\"7 elm ave\"\u2192\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`, and blank-after-normalize \u2192 400) all pass, and nothing in the update (PUT) path was affected.",
